# Code owners: who must review changes to which files.
#
# On its own this file only requests reviews. It becomes binding once the
# ruleset on `main` requires code-owner review, with stale approvals
# dismissed on new commits (docs/agents/dell-setup.md, part A).
#
# The LAST matching line wins, so the specific lines come after the default.
# Every owner listed must have write access to this repository.

# Default: the owner reviews everything.
*                               @DrZaff

# Automations, deploy settings, the database and sign-in. These act outside
# the code once merged (secrets, production builds, access rules).
/.github/                       @DrZaff
/netlify.toml                   @DrZaff
/supabase/                      @DrZaff
/auth.js                        @DrZaff
/scripts/                       @DrZaff

# Clinical content: medical claims, evidence and tool instructions that a
# clinician could act on. A clinician must approve the exact commit.
# The clinical reviewer is the owner (DrZaff, decided 2026-11-06). Agent and
# bot PRs get the owner's clinical approval like any other review; the
# owner's own clinical PRs can't be self-approved, so for logic that could
# change care, add a second clinician's username to the end of the line.
/evidence/                      @DrZaff
/blog/posts/                    @DrZaff
/blog/editorial-queue.json      @DrZaff
/ai-vs-physician.html           @DrZaff
/projects/                      @DrZaff
/games/antibiose.html           @DrZaff
/course-*.html                  @DrZaff
/learn.html                     @DrZaff
